From 0d2b28f3ec430f64482c62abcc3bfb89f8c38ee1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabian Meumertzheim <fabian@meumertzhe.im>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 13:06:40 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Reproduce directory symlinks when prefetching into external
 repos (#31443)

### Description

A repo that is backed by the remote repo contents cache can contain symlinks to directories. When a file or a source directory below such a symlink was prefetched, e.g. `alias/file` with `alias -> real`, the directories along the requested path were created on disk, which turned `alias` into a regular directory.

Both the prefetcher and the materialization of subtrees now resolve symlinks at the directories above the requested path, create the files at the path they resolve to and reproduce the symlinks.

### Motivation

Materializing the entire repo after such a prefetch failed, as the symlink could no longer be created in place of the non-empty directory. This happens, for example, when an action consumes a file below a symlinked directory of a repo and a repo rule later resolves a label in that repo. Until then, the repo on disk also didn't match its cached contents. The added tests fail without the fix.

This is also a prerequisite for recovering files that the remote cache has lost by rewinding repo fetches (#30218, #31197), which completes the materialization of a repo whose files have partially been prefetched.

Work towards #31456

### Build API Changes

No

### Release Notes

RELNOTES: None

Closes #31443

